<title>USA: G7 supports WTO financial services talks.</title>
<headline>G7 supports WTO financial services talks.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-04-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Group of Seven Industrial countries on Sunday they supported the resumption of financial services negotiations in the World Trade Organization.</p>
<p>In a statement issued after G7 ministers meeting, the G7 said that lower barriers among financial markets will contribute to freer flow of capital and accelerate capital market development.</p>
<p>The statement noted that the G7 looked forward to full Most Favored Nation trade agreements between nations based on improved market access commitments and national treatment.</p>
<p>&quot;Accordingly, we will aim to achieve significantly improved market access commitments with a broad level of participation in the agreed upon timeframe,&quot; he said.</p>
</text>
